{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From prey, my son, you ascended.</b> From the root of טרף — you ascended and grew great, for there is no predator and plunderer like you, like ״ואת עלית על כולנה.״ <b>From prey, my son, you ascended.</b> Rashi explained: from the matter in which I suspected you of being the one who tore apart Joseph. But the Sages, may their memory be blessed — as we say in general: what does it profit anyone who blesses Judah? Behold, this is blasphemy. Rather, the interpretation is about Tamar, and the Targum proves it: Judah mounted her not licitly, etc. — from the law of a killing: you endangered your own life, etc. — from the matter of the execution of Tamar and her two sons."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:12.423131017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}